Swift / macOS app
-----------------
The macOS app (apple/) has no Swift Package Manager or CocoaPods dependencies:
it links only Apple system frameworks (AppKit, SwiftUI, Security, Network,
WebKit, CoreSpotlight and similar) and the project's own Rust static library.
There is no Package.resolved. Apple's frameworks are used under the Xcode and
Apple SDK licence terms and are not redistributed here.

Rust core
---------
Third-party Rust crates (native/) are used under their own licences, almost
all MIT or Apache-2.0 (many dual-licensed). Where a crate offers a choice,
this project takes the permissive option:

- mach-sys (GPL-3.0 OR Apache-2.0): used under Apache-2.0.
- r-efi (MIT OR Apache-2.0 OR LGPL-2.1-or-later): used under MIT or Apache-2.0.
- cssparser and dtoa-short (MPL-2.0): used unmodified as dependencies; their
  source remains available from their upstream projects under MPL-2.0.

Run `cargo metadata --manifest-path native/Cargo.toml` (or `cargo license`) for
the full dependency list.

Third-party services
--------------------
Castellum does not ship OAuth client credentials. Users who sign in to Google
or Microsoft mail register their own application (see README.md).
